theorem.raw:
Let $\omega$ be a translation invariant factor state on ${\cal B}$ and $\psi$ be an extremal element in $K_{\omega}$. Then the following statements are equivalent:

\vskip 1em 
\noindent (a) $[{\cal M}^1_0\Omega]=I_{{\cal K}_0},\;[\tilde{{\cal M}}^1_0\Omega]=I_{{\cal K}_0}$;

\vskip 1em 
\noindent (b) $({\cal M}^1_0)'=\tilde{{\cal M}}^1_0$; 

\vskip 1em         
\noindent (c) $\pi_{\omega}({\cal B}_R)'=\pi_{\omega}({\cal B}_L)''$;

\vskip 1em 
\noindent (d) $[\pi_{\omega}({\cal B}_R)'\Omega]=[\pi_{\omega}({\cal B}_L)''\Omega]$;

\vskip 1em 
\noindent (e) $\{x \in {\cal B}({\cal K}): \sum_k \tilde{v}_kx\tilde{v}_k^*= x \} ={\cal M}$; 

\vskip 1em 
\noindent (f) $\omega$ is pure.

\vskip 1em 
In such a case $\tilde{{\cal M}}^1_0 = \{x \in \tilde{{\cal M}}: \beta_z(x)=x: z \in H \}$ where 
$H=\{ z \in S^1:\psi = \psi \beta_z \}$.

